{"chunk_id": "3e16d42b581f", "text": "As Bhishma continues instructing Yudhishthira from his bed of arrows, the king asks a set of ultimate religious questions: Who is the one supreme deity, what refuge should humans seek, what is the highest religion, and what practice frees one from the cycle of birth and death? Bhishma answers by declaring that the supreme refuge is Vishnu\u2014Vasudeva\u2014and that the highest religion is devoted worship of Him. He then begins reciting the celebrated Vishnu\u2011Sahasranama, the thousand names of Vishnu, each describing an attribute, cosmic role, or mythic act: creator, sustainer, witness, destroyer, source of the Vedas, protector of devotees, and incarnations such as Narasimha, Vamana, Rama, and Krishna. The passage emphasizes Vishnu as the all\u2011pervading reality behind creation and liberation, presenting devotional remembrance of His names as a powerful path to spiritual freedom.\nYudhishthira asks the supreme refuge and religion, and Bhishma answers by extolling Vishnu and beginning the recitation of His thousand names.\nThemes: Vishnu\u2019s supremacy, devotional worship, sacred names, liberation from suffering, royal spiritual inquiry", "vector": [0.005595359019935131, -0.016818875446915627, -0.005477285943925381, 0.016031721606850624, -0.009550812654197216, 0.016661444678902626, -0.02282749116420746, -0.01651713252067566, -0.02454611286520958, -0.004772126208990812, 0.011144801042973995, 0.0004095665062777698, 0.02201409824192524, 0.01058067288249731, -0.01042324211448431, -0.009190033189952374, 0.04295241832733154, -0.011623653583228588, 0.027445465326309204, -0.010259252041578293, -0.006592421792447567, -0.00392593489959836, -0.005634716711938381, 0.010593792423605919, -0.01605795882642269, 0.007714117877185345, 0.027917759492993355, -0.012200900353491306, 0.006110289599746466, -0.027025651186704636, -0.012437046505510807, 0.004427745938301086, -0.005890542175620794, 0.005290336441248655, -0.02680262364447117, -0.00